ST-T1024's architectural properties are aligned with the technical requirements underlying DAL C and, with additional work, DAL B. DAL A — the highest-rigor tier, used for catastrophic-failure-class systems like primary flight control — requires redundancy (e.g., triple-redundant FSM) beyond the current single-instance architecture, and is not yet achievable by construction alone.
