The Landscape
ST-T1024 occupies a specific niche: open-source, deterministic, ternary-quantized inference for bounded embedded contexts. This is a different design point than general-purpose accelerators (e.g., GPU/FPGA-based edge AI) or cloud inference platforms, which optimize for different tradeoffs (raw throughput, model flexibility, existing tooling ecosystems). We are not aware of another open-source architecture targeting deterministic, air-gapped, DAL-aligned aerospace inference specifically — but this is a young and fast-moving space, and readers should verify this independently rather than take the claim at face value.
Where This Stands
ST-T1024's architecture is designed around properties — determinism, isolation, auditability, air-gapped operation — that map onto DO-178C's technical requirements more directly than stochastic, cloud-dependent AI does. That architectural alignment is real and, we believe, significant. It is not certification. No formal verification, tool qualification, or independent regulatory assessment has yet been completed. The path from here to an actual certified system runs through the roadmap above, and it has not been shortcut.
